   "evidence": "Fiber.lean:92-94 and 102-103 list `Set.preimage` as a simp lemma. `mathlib/Mathlib/Data/Set/Defs.lean:44-51`: \"Although `Set` is defined as `\u03b1 \u2192 Prop`, this is an implementation detail which should not be relied on. Instead, `Set.ofPred` ... and membership of a set (`\u2208`) should be used.\" The robust replacements exist in the pin: `Nat.card_of_isEmpty` (`Mathlib/SetTheory/Cardinal/Finite.lean:66`, `@[simp]`) and `Nat.card_unique` (`Finite.lean:201`).",
   "file": "TauCeti/Data/Fintype/Fiber.lean",
   "fix": "Avoid sets entirely where possible: for `occCount_of_notMem_range` use `have : IsEmpty {x // f x = y} := \u27e8fun x => h \u27e8x.1, x.2\u27e9\u27e9; simp [occCount_def]` (`Nat.card_of_isEmpty` is simp). For the positive branch of `occCount_of_injective` use uniqueness of the fiber directly: `obtain \u27e8x, rfl\u27e9 := h; have : Unique {x' // f x' = f x} := \u27e8\u27e8\u27e8x, rfl\u27e9\u27e9, fun z => Subtype.ext (hinj z.2)\u27e9; exact Nat.card_unique`, dropping `Nat.card_preimage_of_injective`. If you prefer to keep the preimage route, factor the coercion bridge into one explicit lemma (`occCount_eq_card_preimage : occCount f y = Nat.card (f \u207b\u00b9' {y})`, proved by `Nat.card_congr (Equiv.subtypeEquivRight fun x => by simp)` via `Set.mem_preimage`) and use it in both places instead of repeating the unfolding simp set.",
   "issue": "`occCount_of_notMem_range` closes the goal with `simpa [occCount_def, Set.preimage, Set.coe_ofPred] using congrArg (fun s : Set X => Nat.card s) he`: it unfolds the *definition* `Set.preimage` inside a simp set to identify `\u21a5(f \u207b\u00b9' {y})` with `{x // f x = y}`. Same pattern at line 103 in `occCount_of_injective` (`simpa only [Set.preimage, Set.mem_singleton_iff, Set.coe_ofPred, Nat.card_unique] using hc`). Both are terse but rest on undocumented defeq across the `Set` coercion wrapper.",
   "line": "93"
  }
 ],
